        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How soon can you paint over paintable caulk?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the product. DAP Alex Fast Dry wants 20 minutes before brushing; Alex Plus, Alex Flex and Gorilla Ultimate list 30 minutes. GE's paintable silicone is listed at 30 to 60 minutes. Sashco Big Stretch needs about 4 hours for exterior latex, 1 to 2 days for interior latex and about a week for oil-based paint."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why does my paintable caulk crack after painting?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually because the joint moves more than the caulk is rated for, the bead was laid too deep and shrank, or the paint went on before the caulk had skinned properly. A stiff, cheap flat paint over a stretchy caulk can also crack. Match the caulk's movement rating to the joint, use backer rod on deep gaps and wait the full paint time."
