            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Siliconized acrylic, for most trim. The silicone additive improves adhesion and flexibility, and DAP says it reduces shrinkage compared with plain latex. Plain acrylic painter's caulk is cheaper and fine for static gaps on a big repaint, but it is the type most likely to show a dip or crack under semi-gloss paint at joints that move."
