        <div id="paint-ready" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Paint-Ready Times, Compared
          </h2>

          <p>
            Paint-ready time is the figure most people shop on, and it is the one most often misunderstood. It is the time until a skin forms that is firm enough to brush or roll paint over without dragging the caulk. It is not cure time. The bead underneath is still soft and still losing water for days, which is why a caulk can be paint-ready in 20 minutes and water-ready in 24 hours.
          </p>

